    "reason": "The English lemma 'dream' (noun) in a general context primarily refers to a series of thoughts/images during sleep or a cherished aspiration. The Japanese expression '幻想' (gensou) primarily means 'fantasy,' 'illusion,' or 'vision,' often implying something unreal or imagined. While 'dream' can sometimes encompass 'vision' or 'fantasy,' '幻想' does not cover the most common and natural senses of 'dream' for a general learner (i.e., a dream during sleep or an aspiration). The standard and most natural Japanese word for these primary senses of 'dream' is '夢' (yume).",
